  "rendered": {
    "title": "A self-healing observability pipeline for Aura",
    "intro": "Today's nightly is almost entirely an observability platform push: Aura's status checks gained richer evidence packets, automated source discovery, gated AI-driven repair workflows, and a learning loop that captures lessons across every release. CI guardrails for release history publishing rounded out the day.",
    "entries": [
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-1",
        "time_label": "4:15 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-06-14T11:15:30.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-06-14T11:25:39.000Z",
        "title": "Structured evidence packets for status investigations",
        "summary": "Failed observability checks now produce redacted, contract-aware evidence packets with verifier guidance surfaced through the marketing status view.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Investigations now emit a structured 'aura-observability-investigation-packet' with feature metadata, check contract, sibling-failure patterns, missing required evidence, source hints, and a deterministic reproduction command — all routed through a new redaction layer before leaving the runner.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "64c1782f93bdacb12bfedef98a099cfe3a6c7e24"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Packets gained a verifier-context companion that correlates same-message siblings, flags likely shared-dependency failures, validates against the check expectation contract, and includes inline source excerpts alongside hints.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "0cefae5ced0e299d2b144be32b7e1970564c5d06"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Verifier guidance is now exposed through the marketing status API and StatusView, giving the public status surface a path to show why a check failed instead of just that it failed.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "993166607710cee2eacaca298a629e8c24660ef5"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Added an end-to-end test that exercises the investigations runner against a fake LLM endpoint, locking in the packet and verifier-context payload shape.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "fec3a7a9aa070aa2155bab3088a2046b5f1c6575"
            ],
            "confidence": "medium"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-2",
        "time_label": "8:04 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-06-14T15:04:09.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-06-14T17:02:10.000Z",
        "title": "Gated AI repair loop with automatic dispatch",
        "summary": "A new repair pipeline can investigate failing checks, propose patches with confidence gating, and auto-dispatch a PR-opening workflow from the observability job.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Investigation context now includes a dedicated source-discovery module that ranks candidate code paths, surfaces recent changes, and feeds both evidence packets and verifier probes with concrete file targets.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "76da5873274085e92f72583e63cc947b8ceb0fd2"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Shipped a gated repair loop behind a new aura-observability-repair workflow: it runs probes, investigates failures, and can apply a model-proposed unified diff, open a PR, and run allowlisted verification commands — all guarded by path-prefix and apply/PR toggles.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "8d605c05912b74911325b225af11244c7ce3bf02"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "The main observability workflow now plans and auto-dispatches that repair workflow when investigations clear a configurable minimum-confidence threshold, with PR creation and verification enabled by default for qualifying failures.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "6efed69f7af2f9fa5c2eff57a15a2fd57fdf7ede"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
